            "description": "# Get Execution Errors\n\nThis API endpoint is used to retrieve execution errors for a specific data management definition group in Microsoft Dynamics.\n\n## Request\n\n- Method: POST\n    \n- Endpoint: `{{resource}}data/DataManagementDefinitionGroups/Microsoft.Dynamics.DataEntities.GetExecutionErrors`\n    \n- Headers:\n    \n    - Content-Type: application/json\n        \n    - Authorization: Bearer\n        \n\n### Request Body\n\n- Type: Raw (application/json)\n    \n\n| Key | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| executionId | string | The ID of the execution to retrieve errors for |\n\nExample:\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"executionId\": \"{{generaljournal_execution_id}}\"\n}\n## Response\nThe response for this request will be a JSON object containing the execution errors. Below is the JSON schema for the response:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"errorId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"errorCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"errorMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n    // Add more properties as per the actual response\n  }\n}\n\n ```"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "## General Journal Recurring Import\n\nIf using the example file, follow the steps below:\n\n- Using Contoso setup a recurring import project\n- Set the GenJrn to allocate voucher at posting\n- Set based processing will need to be switch on (default) for the entity General Journal"
    },
